        "pageid": 28566279,
        "ns": 0,
        "title": "A Game of Concentration",
        "extract": "A Game of Concentration (also known as Concentration and Hunt & Score) is a video game programmed by Jim Heuther of Atari, Inc. and released in 1978 for the Atari VCS (later renamed to the Atari 2600). It is a  digital version of the classic memory game played with cards. A Game of Concentration is one of a handful of games that use Atari's keypad controllers.\nThe game was released by Sears for its Tele-Games Video Arcade console under the name Memory Match.",
